    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "description": "Step-by-step demonstration of the Temporal Lending Engine PoC.\n\n## Prerequisites\n1. Temporal Server running on `localhost:7233` (e.g. via `temporal server start-dev`)\n2. Spring Boot app running on `localhost:8080` (e.g. via `./gradlew bootRun` \u2014 this also auto-starts the PostgreSQL container)\n\n## Collection variables\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `baseUrl` | `http://localhost:8080` | Spring Boot base URL |\n| `termLoanId` | *(auto-set)* | ID of the Installments loan created in the Installments folder |\n| `bulletLoanId` | *(auto-set)* | ID of the CDD loan created in the CDD folder |\n| `cancelLoanId` | *(auto-set)* | ID of the loan created in the Cancel Flow folder |\n| `borrowerId` | `borrower-demo-001` | Borrower used for Installments and Cancel Flow scenarios |\n| `bulletBorrowerId` | `borrower-demo-002` | Separate borrower for the CDD scenario (avoids one-active-loan constraint) |\n\n## How to use\nRun each folder **in order** from top to bottom. Within each folder, run requests from Step 1 downward. Test scripts automatically capture IDs from responses and store them as collection variables.",
